          "comment": "1m win in Dubai in January; unplaced both starts since returning to Britain; up against it",
          "spotlight": "Two wins as a 2yo, notably a sales race at Doncaster's St Leger meeting (6.5f, good), and he also won a 1m conditions event in Dubai in January; unplaced in two runs back in Britain this spring/summer and a personal best will be required to take this.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2024-09-12",
              "horse": "Hallasan",
              "horse_id": "hrs_39960270",
              "race": "Weatherbys Scientific £300,000 2-Y-O Stakes (GBB Race)",
              "race_id": "rac_11183627",
              "course": "Doncaster",
              "course_id": "crs_390",
              "distance_f": "6.5",
              "distance_y": "1431",
              "quote": "Will (Buick, jockey) was very pleased with Hallasan and he's toughed it out well. He's a small horse, and we thought he was going to be an early one, but actually he's taken a little while to come to himself. I spoke to the trainer (Charlie Appleby) just now and he thought he might be one to take over to Dubai and see how he goes over there - Alex Merriam, assistant trainer."
            },
            {
              "date": "2024-07-19",
              "horse": "Hallasan",
              "horse_id": "hrs_39960270",
              "race": "Charge Up Your Summer With Rhino.Bet EBF Maiden Stakes (Gbb Race)",
              "race_id": "rac_11325730",
              "course": "Nottingham",
              "course_id": "crs_1040",
              "distance_f": "6",
              "distance_y": "1338",
              "quote": "Hallasan is still a little bit gassy and I think there'll be a bit more improvement to come when he steps into handicap company. He tries hard, so he probably over-tried for the first furlong. Once he relaxed after half a furlong, he found his breathing and rhythm and away he went. I probably could have won hands and heels. He's still learning and this was his second run after becoming a gelding. If there is improvement, I think you'll see it from here on in - Dougie Costello, jockey, speaking to Racing TV."
            }
          ],
