          "prev_owners": [],
          "comment": "3rd to Hucklesbrook at York but not ideally drawn there; still capable of a bigger effort",
          "spotlight": "Much improved this year, winning an AW maiden in fine style on his reappearance and rewarding market support when seeing off his nine rivals at the Craven meeting at Newmarket in April (6f, good to soft); finished the thick end of 3l behind Hucklesbrook at York last month but his high draw wasn't beneficial as things panned out; remains capable of a bigger performance.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2025-04-16",
              "horse": "Double Rush",
              "horse_id": "hrs_44417534",
              "race": "bet365 Handicap",
              "race_id": "rac_11575096",
              "course": "Newmarket",
              "course_id": "crs_988",
              "distance_f": "6",
              "distance_y": "1320",
              "quote": "I think Double Rush is going to be a nice, improving horse through the season. Some of our horses just weren't right last season and he had a nice mark. He probably didn't handle the track today and a flatter track would suit him better. There is a nice valuable handicap at York around a week before Royal Ascot which we could aim at. We will see how he improves and take it step by step. We couldn't put a hand on but the horses just weren't last right season. They looked great but just weren't letting themselves go. They seem nice and healthy this year - Charlie Hills, trainer."
            }
          ],
