          "owner": "Godolphin",
          "owner_id": "own_199380",
          "prev_trainers": [],
          "prev_owners": [],
          "comment": "Talented colt who is 3-4; responded well to first-time hood at Sandown most recently",
          "spotlight": "Unraced as a 2yo; impressive in two Kempton AW contests early this year, looking a 2,000 Guineas prospect; flopped in the Craven, having pulled too hard, but scored comfortably in first-time hood at Sandown (1m, good; Listed) since; talented colt who could well progress further with the headgear retained; respected even with 3lb penalty.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2025-05-29",
              "horse": "Opera Ballo",
              "horse_id": "hrs_49389116",
              "race": "Star Sports Heron Stakes (Listed Race)",
              "race_id": "rac_11621727",
              "course": "Sandown",
              "course_id": "crs_1404",
              "distance_f": "8",
              "distance_y": "1760",
              "quote": "Opera Ballo settled much better than at Newmarket last time and it's good to see him get it done. He's very much a work in progress, the hood has helped a lot. I'm not quite sure what Charlie has planned but he appreciated a bit of juice in the ground and I wouldn't say Royal Ascot is a definite at this stage - Alex Merriam, assistant trainer."
            },
            {
              "date": "2025-02-26",
              "horse": "Opera Ballo",
              "horse_id": "hrs_49389116",
              "race": "\"European Road To The Kentucky Derby\" Conditions Stakes (GBB Race)",
              "race_id": "rac_11535758",
              "course": "Kempton (AW)",
              "course_id": "crs_28054",
              "distance_f": "8",
              "distance_y": "1760",
              "quote": "Opera Ballo was very smooth. I was very pleased with him. I do think he's a work in progress, but it's all there for him - William Buick, jockey, speaking on Racing TV."
            },
            {
              "date": "2025-01-29",
              "horse": "Opera Ballo",
              "horse_id": "hrs_49389116",
              "race": "Unibet Supports Safer Gambling Maiden Stakes (GBB Race) (Div I)",
              "race_id": "rac_11510525",
              "course": "Kempton (AW)",
              "course_id": "crs_28054",
              "distance_f": "8",
              "distance_y": "1760",
              "quote": "Opera Ballo is a beautiful horse. Just watching him going around the paddock was nice and he really impressed me with the way he went about his business. He was very professional. He jumped with the blind, but he got away lovely and I managed to find a nice slot. He was still actually quite green, he overraced a little bit, and he'll probably be better with a little bit of cover going forward, but from the gate it was all about getting him out and into a rhythm. When I asked him to stretch at the two pole, he lengthened away quite quickly and gave me a nice feel. I think another run with experience would definitely benefit him, especially if the option was there to get a mile on some turf. I think it would help getting him to switch off early ? we've seen his finishing kick ? and it could enhance that - Billy Loughnane, jockey, speaking to Racing TV."
            }
          ],
