          "prev_trainers": [],
          "prev_owners": [],
          "comment": "2-2 since racing in Britain; won the Britannia last time; open to further progress",
          "spotlight": "No better than midfield in two Meydan starts; 2-2 since racing in Britain, gamely landing the Britannia at Royal Ascot (1m, good to firm; turf debut) last time, albeit fortuitously as the runner-up looked unlucky; faces a tougher task on these terms but is open to further improvement.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2025-06-19",
              "horse": "Arabian Story",
              "horse_id": "hrs_48667276",
              "race": "Britannia Stakes (Heritage Handicap) (Colts & Geldings)",
              "race_id": "rac_11649755",
              "course": "Ascot",
              "course_id": "crs_52",
              "distance_f": "8",
              "distance_y": "1760",
              "quote": "Arabian Story is doing really good. He came from Dubai and he won first time and today he won as well. We give him a race at Chelmsford and he pleased me and we thought, okay, let's go to Royal Ascot. I talked to Oisin [Murphy, jockey] and said this horse is a mile and a quarter but over the mile you have to be handy with him, you have to give him a chance and he gave him a good ride - Saeed Bin Suroor, trainer.Arabian Story is quite lazy, but he was very good at Chelmsford. He got a little bit of experience in Dubai on the dirt in races he didn't enjoy, which made him tough, and I was delighted with his attitude today. He'll be a Group Three horse going a mile and a quarter. He was the first one off the bridle, and it's very hard to win at Ascot on the straight course when that happens, so he's got a fair level of ability. It's lovely to win one for Saeed [Bin Suroor] - Oisin Murphy, jockey."
            }
          ],
