          "prev_trainers": [],
          "prev_owners": [],
          "comment": "Group 3 C&D win two starts back a career-best; big player back at same level",
          "spotlight": "Late-starter but rapid improver in handicaps last year and has stepped up again this year, making all for 4l win in fillies' Group 3 over C&D in May; found life tougher a fortnight later in Group 2 Lanwades Stud Stakes at the Curragh over a mile, albeit solid run when 3l off classy Porta Fortuna; down in grade and trip and front-runner could take plenty of catching.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2025-05-11",
              "horse": "Vera's Secret",
              "horse_id": "hrs_36824130",
              "race": "Al Shira'aa Racing \"Mutamakina\" Stakes (Group 3) (Fillies & Mares)",
              "race_id": "rac_11615786",
              "course": "Leopardstown",
              "course_id": "crs_4862",
              "distance_f": "7",
              "distance_y": "1593",
              "quote": "Vera's Secret hasn't had a lot of racing and she's a big, strong six-year-old now. She's a quality filly and proved it today. This year, since she came back into training she's been training lovely and relaxing well. Nathan Crosse was to ride her today but he had to go to Hoppegarten for Willie McCreery. He's done a lot of work with her and she's his ride so we were lucky to get Seamie today. She's entered in the Lanwades on Guineas weekend and we'll probably come back for the Matron Stakes later in the year. She's a bit different this year, more mature and she'll come on for this as she's over 600 kilos and takes plenty of work at home - John Feane, trainer."
            },
            {
              "date": "2024-07-21",
              "horse": "Vera's Secret",
              "horse_id": "hrs_36824130",
              "race": "Irish Stallion Farms EBF Fillies Handicap",
              "race_id": "rac_11345880",
              "course": "Curragh",
              "course_id": "crs_4628",
              "distance_f": "8",
              "distance_y": "1760",
              "quote": "Vera's Secret is a filly we like a lot. It's good that she did things properly today. She wasn't too keen. I think they all wanted to move to the middle and it suited her as she got a freebie and got to prick her ears - John Feane, trainer."
            }
          ],
